# Git

- Branches: `main` (production), `develop` (integration), `feature/AW-XXX-name`, `fix/AW-XXX-name`, `hotfix/*`.
- Conventional commits with scope and issue ID:

```text
feat(lead): add automatic lead assignment [AW-031]
fix(booking): prevent duplicate slot booking [AW-142]
docs(tenant): update tenant resolution architecture
test(rbac): add cross-tenant authorization tests
security(auth): rate limit password reset
```

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `security`.
- One logical change per commit. Review `git diff` before committing.
- Before committing: `php artisan test`, `vendor/bin/pint --test`, `npm run build` all pass.
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, `public/build/`.
- Never force-push shared branches (`main`, `develop`). Never rewrite published history.
- Do not push or open PRs unless the user asks.
